      "documentConcept": "Salesforce single-subscriber durable MongoDB alert distribution",
      "canonicalConceptId": "concept:6b39dd09c9869078983cc22b6b22325eff82d5a0bd79c8b77bfe51c7ed828027",
      "text": "A proposed distribution architecture uses one Salesforce subscription to persist an inbox in MongoDB, then distributes application alerts from committed database changes. Salesforce replay supports recovery within a finite retention window. MongoDB transactions can couple durable intake with checkpoint updates, while change streams supply live notifications. Neither replay positions nor notifications establish exactly-once application delivery. Consumers need idempotent processing, and alert records must remain queryable when change-stream history is unavailable. The combined architecture is a design inference from vendor primitives; the cited Wolverine repository supplies an analogous durable Salesforce inbox for platform events, not a MongoDB Case implementation.",
      "sources": [
        "https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/platform/pub-sub-api/guide/event-message-durability.html",
